    "finding": "Pinned Mathlib already provides genuine one-dimensional CLT and, more directly, its public characteristic-function Taylor limit. A finite product/count Rademacher producer can reuse this leaf without porting SLT LevyContinuity or constructing an infinite iid sample space. Entropy convergence is then a bounded-continuous integral corollary. Full flip-energy limit4 remains a separate secant/exchangeability producer.",
    "one_exact_next_target": {
      "proposed_name": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Probability.BalancedRademacherCLT.balanced_count_sum_tendsto_gaussian",
      "statement": "Let mu_N be the ACTUAL uniform probability on (Fin N -> Bool), normalized by cardinal2^N; sign(false)=-1,sign(true)=1, S_N(eps)=(sqrt(N))^-1*sum_i sign(eps_i). Define lambda_N=(mu_N).map S_N as an internally derived ProbabilityMeasure R. Prove Tendsto (fun n => lambda_(n+1)) atTop (nhds <gaussianReal0,1,probability>). No CLT/limit/law/domain/normalizer certificate binder.",
      "consumer": "The actual compact-C2 entropy of f(S_N)^2 in Bernoulli LSI, together with actual derivative-square weak-law convergence for the flip-energy parent. This is a proposed target, not claimed or compiled."
    },
    "ready_status": "API-ready route proposal; exact count-to-real-product law adapter and actual moments must still be implemented. Current34 n2 tests do not discharge any all-n or limiting statement."
  },
