  "minimal_route_at_most7_steps": [
    "1. Build actual mu_N finite balanced-count probability and measurable S_N. Prove coordinate-sign pushforward nu=(1/2)delta_-1+(1/2)delta_1 and actual joint sign map =Measure.pi(const nu); consequently lambda_N equals the normalized sum pushforward of nu^N. Prove nu moment0 and moment2=1 directly from two atoms; no supplied probability or moment assumptions.",
    "2. Use ProbabilityTheory.charFun_map_sum_pi_eq_prod plus MeasureTheory.charFun_map_mul_comp to identify charFun(lambda_N)(t)=(charFun nu((sqrtN)^-1*t))^N. Apply ProbabilityTheory.tendsto_charFun_inv_sqrt_mul_pow with P=nu,X=id, actual moments and measurability; this reuses the genuine Mathlib CLT proof leaf and avoids both infinitePi/iid adapters and a new cosine Taylor port.",
    "3. Identify target characteristic function by ProbabilityTheory.charFun_gaussianReal at mean0,variance1; apply MeasureTheory.ProbabilityMeasure.tendsto_iff_tendsto_charFun and shift n->n+1. The actual target is gaussianReal0,1, not variance1/2 or an opaque covariance convention. This proves the next actual law producer.",
    "4. For real C2 compact-support f, internally produce bounded-continuous f², f²log(f²), and (derivf)². Derivative compact support uses HasCompactSupport.deriv, derivative continuity uses C2; log0 handled via Real.continuous_mul_log. Apply ProbabilityMeasure.tendsto_iff_forall_integral_tendsto to the proved actual laws. Subtract mass*logmass using continuous_mul_log including mass0: actual entropy convergence, no entropy-limit premise.",
    "5. For N>=1 define actual coordinate flip eps^i and rescaled secant A_N,i= sqrtN/(2*sign eps_i)*(f(S_N)-f(S_N(eps^i))). Actual displacement=2sign(eps_i)/sqrtN. Derive bounded B=sup|fprime|,K=sup|fsecond| from compact C2. Mean value theorem and derivative Lipschitz give |A²-fprime(S_N)²|<=4BK/sqrtN; all finite-count integrals are genuine L1 and bounds, not totalized uncertified terms.",
    "6. Use actual coordinate permutation of uniform count law to make every flip integral equal. Hence full energy=sum_i int(f(S_N)-f(S_Nflip_i))²=N*int(firstflipdiff)². The true comparison error to4*int fprime(S_N)² is at most16BK/sqrtN, tending0. Combine step4 derivative-square weak integral limit to prove exact full flip-energy limit4*int_gaussianReal0,1 fprime². No finalcomparison/energy-limit binder.",
    "7. Join the actual proved Bernoulli inequality half coefficient with step4 entropy and step6 full energy using le_of_tendsto_of_tendsto. This yields compact-C2 real GaussianLSI constant2. Finite-product tensorization/orthonormal Gaussian adapter and actual32 noncompact C2 cutoff entropy/energy convergence remain distinct producers before general finite-Hilbert sourceKL/LSI/T2 conclusions."
  ],
